# sprint-implementation (drone-navigation)

Paths below resolve from the repository root. Read `AGENTS.md` and the canonical
constitution at `../buildtwin/.specify/memory/constitution.md` before work. Follow its compatibility,
test-first, data-preservation, and evidence rules; report conflicts and preserve unrelated changes.

MUST:
- TDD: failing pytest in `tests/` before implementation
- test subject named `sut`
- test name: `test_should_{outcome}_when_{condition}`
- English-only: branches, commits, identifiers, test names
- geometry/algorithms in `navigation/core/`; thin FastAPI routes in `app/api/routes/`
- branch: `{type}/{english-kebab-slug}` from `main`

NEVER:
- code comments in production or test code
- non-English branch/commit/identifier names
- edit existing test before classifying failure

TEST_BROKEN:
- Classify failures before editing tests; distinguish regressions, pre-existing defects, and blockers
- Fix implementation when it violates accepted requirements; never delete, skip, or weaken tests to pass
- Explain expectation changes with accepted requirements or evidence of a test error; internal
  refactors must preserve observable contract expectations
- Reproduce defects; verify permitted-success and forbidden-action cases plus affected contracts

REF: ../buildtwin/docs/SPRINT-WORKFLOW.md
